Audio: skip PDR on this Wi-Fi-only device, saving five minutes of every boot.

WHAT IT COSTS TODAY
-------------------
There is no sound card for the first five and a half minutes after boot, on
every boot. Not a slow card: no card at all, and nothing userspace does can
create one before then.

WHY
---
audio_notifier prefers PDR over SSR for the ADSP domain. PDR needs the
servreg_locator QMI service, and on Qualcomm platforms that service is hosted by
the MODEM. This tablet is Wi-Fi-only: /sys/bus/msm_subsys reports `modem` as
OFFLINING on every boot and nothing ever starts it.

So the locator never appears, and drivers/soc/qcom/service-locator.c waits out
its entire LOCATOR_SERVICE_TIMEOUT of 300000 ms before giving up:

    servloc: pd_locator_work: Unable to connect to service locator!, rc = -62

measured on gts7fewifi at t = 316.38 s. Until that fires, PDR_ADSP sits at
UNINIT_SERVICE and audio_notifier_reg_client() takes its "if a service is not
initialized, wait for it to come up" branch, so apr is registered with NOTHING.

That matters more than a delayed notification, because apr_adsp_up() is the only
caller of of_platform_populate() for the soc:qcom,msm-audio-apr node:

    spin_lock(&apr_priv->apr_lock);
    if (apr_priv->is_initial_boot)
            schedule_work(&apr_priv->add_chld_dev_work);
    spin_unlock(&apr_priv->apr_lock);

No subscription means no up event, which means qcom,q6core-audio and the `sound`
device under it are never created, which means the qcom,lahaina-asoc-snd machine
driver has nothing to bind and there is no card. Measured: ADSP power-ups at
t = 70, 170, 275 and 311 s each took the DSP to ONLINE and produced zero apr
children; the same write after the timeout produced all fifteen instantly.

THE FIX
-------
Ask for SSR directly for the ADSP domain. SSR delivers the same up and down
notifications through subsys_notif and is available from probe. The only thing
PDR adds is per-protection-domain granularity, which nothing on this device
uses.

audio_notifier_reg_client() walks services downward from the default, and SSR is
index 0, so returning SSR simply registers there and never consults PDR. The
modem domain is untouched; it already defaults to SSR.

SHIPPING
--------
audio_notifier.c builds into q6_notifier_dlkm.ko, a MODULE on the rootfs, so
this does not need a flash: build the kernel package and push that one file.

The pr_info is deliberate, not debug noise. Userspace needs to know which
service was chosen: 72-audio-bringup.start behaves completely differently on a
kernel that still waits out the PDR timeout, and inferring that from the absence
of a log line is exactly the kind of guess that has gone wrong on this port
before. One line, once, at client registration.

VERIFY
------
    # card should exist within seconds of boot, not at ~340 s
    grep -c lahaina /proc/asound/cards
    dmesg | grep "Q6 is Up"
    logger output of 72-audio-bringup.start should no longer wait for the
    locator message at all

--- a/techpack/audio/dsp/audio_notifier.c
+++ b/techpack/audio/dsp/audio_notifier.c
@@ -109,7 +109,39 @@
 	/* initial service to connect per domain */
 	switch (domain) {
 	case AUDIO_NOTIFIER_ADSP_DOMAIN:
-		service = AUDIO_NOTIFIER_PDR_SERVICE;
+		/*
+		 * PDR is unreachable on a Wi-Fi-only device and costs five
+		 * minutes of every boot, so go straight to SSR.
+		 *
+		 * PDR needs the servreg_locator QMI service, which is hosted by
+		 * the MODEM. This tablet has no modem: /sys/bus/msm_subsys
+		 * reports it OFFLINING on every boot and nothing ever starts
+		 * it. So the locator never appears and service-locator.c waits
+		 * out its full LOCATOR_SERVICE_TIMEOUT of 300000 ms:
+		 *
+		 *   servloc: pd_locator_work: Unable to connect to service
+		 *            locator!, rc = -62
+		 *
+		 * measured at t = 316.38 s. Until that fires, PDR_ADSP sits at
+		 * UNINIT_SERVICE, audio_notifier_reg_client() takes its
+		 * "wait for it to come up" branch, and apr is subscribed to
+		 * NOTHING. apr_adsp_up() therefore never runs, and since it is
+		 * the only caller of of_platform_populate() for the
+		 * msm-audio-apr node, qcom,q6core-audio and the `sound` device
+		 * under it are never created and there is no sound card at all.
+		 *
+		 * The practical effect was that audio appeared five and a half
+		 * minutes into every boot, and only because userspace waited
+		 * for that log line before booting the DSP.
+		 *
+		 * SSR gives the same up/down notifications through
+		 * subsys_notif and works from probe. Nothing on this device
+		 * uses per-protection-domain granularity, which is the only
+		 * thing PDR adds.
+		 */
+		pr_info("%s: using SSR for ADSP (PDR skipped: no modem on this device)\n",
+			__func__);
+		service = AUDIO_NOTIFIER_SSR_SERVICE;
 		break;
 	case AUDIO_NOTIFIER_MODEM_DOMAIN:
 		service = AUDIO_NOTIFIER_SSR_SERVICE;
